The two repetitions at both sizes encode a 17-byte frozen-header draft, three 68-byte Free drafts and two 41-byte relations, totaling 303 encoding Work. Their staging charges are respectively 307, three times 460 and twice 379, totaling 2,445: three times the encoded bytes plus six 256-unit record allowances. Containment additionally counts shared declaration authority, so the header contributes 952 bytes at three declarations and 7,702 at 33, and the complete pending draft totals are 3,090 and 9,840 bytes. These are pending-draft amounts, not complete admission peak ceilings. The fixed 256-unit journal checkpoint and six draft visits remain separate. Draft lengths and local-reference positions are schema-dependent, but their records, copies, undo entries and publication still belong to each new graph; retaining their measured length would not eliminate those operations or current containment checks under (`ex:nrz:quantity-registration-residual-work`), (`[BINDINGS-ex:bindings:frozen-registration-cost-separation]`), (`[BINDINGS-ex:bindings:quantity-registration-transaction-cost]`), (`[CAS-rule:cas:registration-template-publication]`).

