Two fresh repetitions of the byte-metered experiment reproduce used-name costs of 46, 23 and 46 Work at three declarations and 72, 49 and 26 at 33, totaling 115 and 147 instead of 2,304 and 5,376. Fresh registration measures 5,681 instead of 7,870 and 7,963 instead of 13,192; unchanged freeze costs would make complete first use 8,727 and 75,203. The current complete census contains 128 affected tests rather than the earlier 110: 105 falling Work assertions, 22 bounded-outcome changes and one changed exhaustion diagnostic, with every first failure recorded by (`[CAS-ex:cas:declaration-lookup-failure-census]`). The full-ladder test retains its ReplayWork refusal at the same limit and phase while its needed value rises from 2,000,017 to 2,000,080, so implementation remains deferred under (`[CAS-cav:cas:lookup-refusal-diagnostic]`), (`[MATRIX-test:integration:integrated-full-ladder-retains-symbolic-work-refusal]`). These are experimental figures, not changed pins; retain the verified header-key segment and the proposed consumption policy of (`dec:nrz:quantity-lookup-consumption`) under (`ex:nrz:quantity-registration-name-allowance`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-registration-accounting`), (`[CAS-ex:cas:registration-byte-lookup-experiment]`).

**Decision (Consume actual declaration lookup Work)** · `dec:nrz:quantity-lookup-consumption`

Propose incremental consumption for the declaration lookup change, with adoption still open pending the category (c) review: charge each compared UTF-8 byte pair immediately against the active cumulative caller allowance, retain earlier Work on refusal, and reserve or refund nothing inside lookup. An empty-key comparison has a one-unit minimum and an empty table costs zero; ordinary byte and length ordering and the binary search path remain unchanged. This policy applies to all header and validation consumers, with unchanged environment authentication, requested-sort checks and transactional publication. Refusal reports the attempted next cumulative charge in the active ledger, translating both limit and needed to the same replay origin where required; a smaller total cost can move the first refused downstream charge and increase needed without implying an increase in complete execution cost, as specified by (`[CAS-rule:cas:declaration-lookup-refusal-reporting]`), (`[CAS-ex:cas:declaration-lookup-exhaustion-prefix]`). The measured registration figures remain experimental until the complete failure inventory, bounded-outcome review and literal boundary twins satisfy (`dec:nrz:quantity-registration-lookup-accounting`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-registration-accounting`), (`[CAS-dec:cas:declaration-lookup-consumption]`), (`[CAS-rule:cas:declaration-lookup-allowance]`), (`[CAS-rule:cas:declaration-lookup-authority]`), (`[CAS-crit:cas:declaration-lookup-adoption]`).

