Numerical materialization of an exact count ratio must choose an explicit scalar format and invoke the existing matrix numerical authority while retaining both original count operands, their exact source evidence and the nonzero-divisor obligation. It must carry representation error inside a complete total, preserve descriptor and companion targets, and refuse atomically with monotone caller Work; it must not relabel a continuous expectation or standard uncertainty as an exact tally. The implemented numerical boundary is (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:count-ratio-numerical-import]`), with remaining scope at (`[MATRIX-cav:matrix:exact-count-ratio-materialization]`), under (`rule:nrz:quantity-heap-counts`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-heap-conversions`), (`req:nrz:quantity-heap-evidence`).

