An exact count array must own ordered exact integer elements outside floating arenas, retain the checked counted-kind descriptor and original source evidence, and use checked extents solely as structural metadata. Addition, subtraction, integer scaling and exact partition operate elementwise after shape and counted-kind agreement, check each actual mathematical result and executable capacity, and publish a complete immutable array only after every element succeeds. One fractional, overflowing, out-of-domain or exhausted element refuses the whole operation while retaining spent Work and every original operand. The implemented boundary has fresh-store literal Work/storage boundaries and independent scalar oracles at (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:exact-count-array-arithmetic]`), (`[MATRIX-ex:matrix:count-array-costs]`) under (`rule:vision:counts-and-metadata`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-heap-counts`), (`req:nrz:quantity-heap-evidence`), (`[MATRIX-req:matrix:exact-count-arrays]`).

