The array container shares existing immutable scalar count nodes in checked column order, rather than copying their integers into a second representation. A checked count source supplies homogeneous counted-kind authority for every shape, including empty arrays, without contributing an implicit element. Scalar count arithmetic remains the sole value/domain checker; the container reserves its source, handles and all prepared element lineages before publishing the complete result. This ownership decision refines (`req:nrz:quantity-count-arrays`), (`rule:vision:counts-and-metadata`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-count-implementation`) through (`[MATRIX-dec:matrix:count-array-ownership]`).

## Nonlinear scalar quantities · `sec:nrz:quantity-nonlinear`

**Rule (Nonlinear dimensions and coordinate measures)** · `rule:nrz:quantity-nonlinear-measures`

Bindings derives product and quotient dimensions by exact exponent addition and subtraction, integer powers by multiplication by the exact integer, and square roots by multiplication by `1/2`. CAS reduction makes `2/4` identical to `1/2`; registry admission still refuses fractional result dimensions under an integral-only policy and exponents outside its supported exact range. Coordinate measures compose without implicit conversion: product scale `s_x s_y`, quotient scale `s_x/s_y`, integer-power scale `s_x^n`, and root scale `sqrt(s_x)`, each with zero difference offset and an exact retained definition. An unsupported exact scale construction refuses instead of substituting a rounded scale. These requirements extend (`rule:nrz:quantity-heap-arithmetic`), (`def:vision:dimensions`), (`def:vision:measures`), (`req:vision:powers-and-factor-dimensions`) through (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:quantity-nonlinear-measures]`).

**Rule (Nonlinear kinds, points and counts)** · `rule:nrz:quantity-nonlinear-kinds`

Only plain continuous values with difference role and explicitly admitted ordered kind relations enter multiplication, division, integer powers or roots. Equal dimensions never infer a result kind. A point refuses even at zero offset or exponent zero; an explicit compatible origin must first produce a difference, including the distinguished absolute-zero origin for multiplicative absolute temperature. Converting a point to coherent coordinates alone does not suffice. An exact count times a quantity is a separately checked scaling operation retaining the count source and exact integer; it is never an implicit count-to-ratio cast or a floating count import. This refines (`rule:vision:semantic-kinds-and-roles`), (`rule:vision:measure-conversions`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-heap-counts`) through (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:quantity-nonlinear-kinds]`).

**Rule (Nonlinear companion enclosure)** · `rule:nrz:quantity-nonlinear-companions`

The complete deterministic input interval and the numerical-only interval propagate separately through the existing certified sum, product, reciprocal and positive-square-root kernels. The complete total contains every prior and new numerical error once, including intermediate reciprocal, repeated-product and coordinate-packing errors; dependency relaxation may widen the bound but cannot omit interaction. A product covers the full Cartesian operand boxes, a quotient composes reciprocal then product, and integer powers retain every executed product and any reciprocal. Statistical quantity products use separately checked Jacobian evidence under (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:quantity-product-covariance-support]`) and report linearized covariance. Integer powers use (`rule:nrz:quantity-power-covariance-support`); quotients and roots use (`rule:nrz:quantity-nonlinear-covariance-support`); uncertainty-valued arithmetic retains `NonlinearStatistics`; no nonlinear covariance is presented as exact. These obligations follow (`rule:vision:uncertainty-unit-algebra`), (`def:nrz:cas-enclosures-existing-kernels`), (`[SCALAR-def:scalar:kernel-certificate]`), (`[SCALAR-rule:scalar:kernel-certificate-relations]`), (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:quantity-nonlinear-companions]`).

**Rule (Nonlinear numerical domains)** · `rule:nrz:quantity-nonlinear-domains`

Division and negative powers require a certified divisor enclosure excluding zero. A square root requires certified nonnegative input coverage, and the currently available exported root certificate imposes the stricter positive-lower-endpoint condition: zero-touching boxes remain an explicit `PositiveRoot` refusal until a separate certificate admits them. Negative or zero-straddling radicands refuse; no endpoint is clamped. The result of `sqrt(2 m²)` must carry an enclosure whose squared endpoints bracket two, never a rounded center presented as exact. Domain checks apply to both total and numerical-only targets under (`rule:nrz:quantity-nonlinear-companions`), (`[SCALAR-rule:scalar:kernel-certificate-relations]`), (`[CAS-rule:cas:scalar-kernel-certificate]`), (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:quantity-nonlinear-domains]`).

**Requirement (Nonlinear evidence and publication)** · `req:nrz:quantity-nonlinear-evidence`

Each result retains the original ordered operands, their exact descriptors, selected value and companion versions, the frozen declaration authority and every executed kernel certificate; a unary result retains its original operand and exact exponent where applicable. Fresh value, total-bound and numerical-error symbols register through the retained frozen environment. All semantic, domain, resource and numerical checks precede atomic heap publication, and refusal retains spent monotone Work without publishing a prefix. Each operation requires fresh-store cold and explicitly warm literal `N`/`N−1` boundaries, independent exact rational or squared-root oracles, and acceptance twins for point, statistical, zero-divisor, negative-root and exponent-policy refusals under (`req:nrz:quantity-heap-evidence`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-registration-freshness`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-registration-accounting`), (`[MATRIX-req:matrix:quantity-nonlinear-evidence]`).

