Repeated compatible quantity operations must reuse a checked descriptor-level sensitivity identity from ordinary published provenance instead of constructing and replaying it per numerical call. The key retains the frozen rule authority, recipe revision, complete non-Work symbolic policy and exact ordered descriptors; every new operating point still receives an independently evaluated Jacobian and numerical error, with current source and covariance capture. Failed operations cannot publish reusable entries. This requirement follows the measured symbolic-versus-numerical separation at (`[MATRIX-ex:matrix:quantity-covariance-derivative-baseline]`) and the bounded lookup contract at (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:quantity-covariance-proof-reuse]`) under (`rule:nrz:quantity-covariance-jacobians`), (`req:nrz:quantity-covariance-evidence`).

